From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cryptohome: a NickelOS local account owns its vault

A local account (<name>@nickel.localhost) is the Linux user <name>, and
its session runs Chrome as that user, so the user owns the vault's
directories (user home, MyFiles, Downloads, caches, skeleton files) where
chronos did. The group stays chronos-access where it was; other accounts'
vaults, the root home and /home/chronos itself are unchanged. The owner is
looked up per mount from the account id the mount is for.

---
diff -ruN a/cryptohome/namespace_mounter/mounter.cc b/cryptohome/namespace_mounter/mounter.cc
--- a/cryptohome/namespace_mounter/mounter.cc
+++ b/cryptohome/namespace_mounter/mounter.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
